     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That's twice the maximum labeled daily dose, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe intended order may have been one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at a different frequency\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest verifying it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
